1.What is Input Layer? Explain its role in ANN.
The first layer of the network where raw data enters.
For example - For image classification, each pixel value becomes an input neuron.

2.What is Hidden Layer? Why is it called hidden?
Layer between input and output layer where transformation occurs using weight and activation function its hidden not directly visible to user.

3.What is Output Layer? Explain its purpose.
The final layer that produces the network predictions.
Its size depend on - 
Binary Classification - 1 node (eg. Yes/No)
Multi-class classification - N nodes (softmax gives probabilities)

4.Why are hidden layers important in Deep Learning?
They enable network to learn non linear relationship
Without them model will behave like linear regression.

5.How many hidden layers make a network “Deep”?
A network is consider deep when it has two or more hidden layers.
More layers - more abstraction - better feature extraction.

6.What operations happen in Input Layer?
Normalization or scaling of input data.
Passing input values forward to the first hidden layer.

7.What operations happen in Hidden Layer?
Weighted sum of inputs -> activation function -> output to next layer.
Example - y=f(wx+b) , where f is activation function like ReLU or sigmoid.

8.What happens in Output Layer during prediction?
Combine signals from the last hidden layer to produce final output.
Often uses softmax (multi class) or sigmoid (for binary) activation.

